[
{
"start": 19.873,
"end": 24.885,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "Notion replaces the dozen tools your team only half uses.",
"char_start": 14,
"char_end": 71,
"unit_id": "t0002.u01",
"sent_id": "t0002.s02"
},
{
"start": 24.885,
"end": 26.732,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "Try notion.com today.",
"char_start": 72,
"char_end": 93,
"unit_id": "t0002.u01",
"sent_id": "t0002.s03"
},
{
"start": 26.732,
"end": 36.462,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "Before we get started, Lena Hofmann was on the last episode and said that tire pressure is more important than suspension adjustments.",
"char_start": 94,
"char_end": 228,
"unit_id": "t0002.u01",
"sent_id": "t0002.s04"
},
{
"start": 36.462,
"end": 37.398,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "Yes, exactly.",
"char_start": 244,
"char_end": 257,
"unit_id": "t0003.u01",
"sent_id": "t0003.s01"
},
{
"start": 37.398,
"end": 41.0,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "And that connects to what we are discussing today.",
"char_start": 258,
"char_end": 308,
"unit_id": "t0003.u01",
"sent_id": "t0003.s02"
},
{
"start": 41.0,
"end": 46.979,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "I'd like to point something out \u2013 Lena Hofmann mentioned the same dynamic a few episodes ago.",
"char_start": 323,
"char_end": 416,
"unit_id": "t0004.u01",
"sent_id": "t0004.s01"
},
{
"start": 46.979,
"end": 53.025,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "I'd like to point something out \u2013 Stefan Brandt mentioned the same dynamic a few episodes ago.",
"char_start": 417,
"char_end": 511,
"unit_id": "t0004.u01",
"sent_id": "t0004.s02"
},
{
"start": 53.025,
"end": 54.708,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "I want to delve deeper into that.",
"char_start": 512,
"char_end": 545,
"unit_id": "t0004.u01",
"sent_id": "t0004.s03"
},
{
"start": 54.708,
"end": 58.738,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "What did you believe about it previously, and what have you revised since then?",
"char_start": 546,
"char_end": 625,
"unit_id": "t0004.u01",
"sent_id": "t0004.s04"
},
{
"start": 58.738,
"end": 69.084,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "In most cases, the mysterious creaking noises can be resolved by cleaning the contact surfaces and tightening them to the specified torque.",
"char_start": 641,
"char_end": 780,
"unit_id": "t0005.u01",
"sent_id": "t0005.s01"
},
{
"start": 69.084,
"end": 73.252,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "We've seen this work with teams that use Spoke & Wrench.",
"char_start": 781,
"char_end": 837,
"unit_id": "t0005.u01",
"sent_id": "t0005.s02"
},
{
"start": 73.252,
"end": 79.058,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "The framing is important because it tells you what compromises you are making.",
"char_start": 838,
"char_end": 916,
"unit_id": "t0005.u01",
"sent_id": "t0005.s03"
},
{
"start": 79.058,
"end": 80.937,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "This is a useful framework.",
"char_start": 931,
"char_end": 958,
"unit_id": "t0006.u01",
"sent_id": "t0006.s01"
},
{
"start": 80.937,
"end": 84.626,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "Where do maintenance and the drive mechanism overlap?",
"char_start": 959,
"char_end": 1012,
"unit_id": "t0006.u01",
"sent_id": "t0006.s02"
},
{
"start": 84.626,
"end": 86.223,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "That's my perspective.",
"char_start": 1028,
"char_end": 1050,
"unit_id": "t0007.u01",
"sent_id": "t0007.s01"
},
{
"start": 86.223,
"end": 93.045,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "A bike should feel quiet and predictable, so that your attention remains focused on the trail.",
"char_start": 1051,
"char_end": 1145,
"unit_id": "t0007.u01",
"sent_id": "t0007.s02"
},
{
"start": 93.045,
"end": 97.835,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "And the second-order effect is the part that most people overlook.",
"char_start": 1146,
"char_end": 1212,
"unit_id": "t0007.u01",
"sent_id": "t0007.s03"
},
{
"start": 97.835,
"end": 99.988,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "I want to delve deeper into that.",
"char_start": 1227,
"char_end": 1260,
"unit_id": "t0008.u01",
"sent_id": "t0008.s01"
},
{
"start": 99.988,
"end": 104.948,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "What is the structural perspective that most listeners don't have access to?",
"char_start": 1261,
"char_end": 1337,
"unit_id": "t0008.u01",
"sent_id": "t0008.s02"
},
{
"start": 104.948,
"end": 105.657,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "Certainly.",
"char_start": 1353,
"char_end": 1363,
"unit_id": "t0009.u01",
"sent_id": "t0009.s01"
},
{
"start": 105.657,
"end": 111.397,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "Chain wear is the best early indicator of when you need to replace your cassette.",
"char_start": 1364,
"char_end": 1445,
"unit_id": "t0009.u01",
"sent_id": "t0009.s02"
},
{
"start": 111.397,
"end": 115.012,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "We've seen this with teams that use Spoke & Wrench.",
"char_start": 1446,
"char_end": 1497,
"unit_id": "t0009.u01",
"sent_id": "t0009.s03"
},
{
"start": 115.012,
"end": 120.469,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "The framing is important because it tells you what compromises you're making.",
"char_start": 1498,
"char_end": 1575,
"unit_id": "t0009.u01",
"sent_id": "t0009.s04"
},
{
"start": 120.469,
"end": 121.963,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "Tell me more about it.",
"char_start": 1590,
"char_end": 1612,
"unit_id": "t0010.u01",
"sent_id": "t0010.s01"
},
{
"start": 121.963,
"end": 126.956,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "Spoke & Wrench is one of the platforms where this becomes clearly visible.",
"char_start": 1628,
"char_end": 1702,
"unit_id": "t0011.u01",
"sent_id": "t0011.s01"
},
{
"start": 126.956,
"end": 130.599,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "I have observed this pattern in three different teams.",
"char_start": 1703,
"char_end": 1757,
"unit_id": "t0011.u01",
"sent_id": "t0011.s02"
},
{
"start": 130.599,
"end": 132.83,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "Tell me how you made your decision.",
"char_start": 1772,
"char_end": 1807,
"unit_id": "t0012.u01",
"sent_id": "t0012.s01"
},
{
"start": 132.83,
"end": 135.379,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "How does RockShox fit into this picture?",
"char_start": 1808,
"char_end": 1848,
"unit_id": "t0012.u01",
"sent_id": "t0012.s02"
},
{
"start": 135.379,
"end": 135.701,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "Sure.",
"char_start": 1864,
"char_end": 1869,
"unit_id": "t0013.u01",
"sent_id": "t0013.s01"
},
{
"start": 135.701,
"end": 141.182,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "Service intervals for the suspension are a decision made by the risk management team.",
"char_start": 1870,
"char_end": 1955,
"unit_id": "t0013.u01",
"sent_id": "t0013.s02"
},
{
"start": 141.182,
"end": 145.824,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "If you ignore that, you'll have to rebuild it from scratch a year later.",
"char_start": 1956,
"char_end": 2028,
"unit_id": "t0013.u01",
"sent_id": "t0013.s03"
},
{
"start": 145.824,
"end": 146.733,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "Guess what?",
"char_start": 2043,
"char_end": 2054,
"unit_id": "t0014.u01",
"sent_id": "t0014.s01"
},
{
"start": 146.733,
"end": 152.185,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "I'll just say it: Linear manages my entire engineering operations.",
"char_start": 2055,
"char_end": 2121,
"unit_id": "t0014.u01",
"sent_id": "t0014.s02"
},
{
"start": 152.185,
"end": 158.134,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "Linear is the issue tracker built for speed \u2013 designed for keyboard use.",
"char_start": 2122,
"char_end": 2194,
"unit_id": "t0014.u01",
"sent_id": "t0014.s03"
},
{
"start": 158.134,
"end": 160.695,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "Use the link in the show notes.",
"char_start": 2195,
"char_end": 2226,
"unit_id": "t0014.u01",
"sent_id": "t0014.s04"
},
{
"start": 160.695,
"end": 164.236,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "We'll be right back, after a short advertisement.",
"char_start": 2227,
"char_end": 2276,
"unit_id": "t0014.u01",
"sent_id": "t0014.s05"
},
{
"start": 181.31,
"end": 183.526,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "Welcome back to the show.",
"char_start": 2277,
"char_end": 2302,
"unit_id": "t0016.u01",
"sent_id": "t0016.s01"
},
{
"start": 183.526,
"end": 185.407,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "That's a helpful framework.",
"char_start": 2303,
"char_end": 2330,
"unit_id": "t0016.u01",
"sent_id": "t0016.s02"
},
{
"start": 185.407,
"end": 189.1,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "Where do maintenance and the drive mechanism overlap?",
"char_start": 2331,
"char_end": 2384,
"unit_id": "t0016.u01",
"sent_id": "t0016.s03"
},
{
"start": 189.1,
"end": 190.763,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "That's my understanding.",
"char_start": 2400,
"char_end": 2424,
"unit_id": "t0017.u01",
"sent_id": "t0017.s01"
},
{
"start": 190.763,
"end": 199.425,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "Most mysterious creaking noises can be resolved by cleaning the contact surfaces and tightening them to the specified torque.",
"char_start": 2425,
"char_end": 2550,
"unit_id": "t0017.u01",
"sent_id": "t0017.s02"
},
{
"start": 199.425,
"end": 203.722,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "We've seen this happen with teams that use Shimano components.",
"char_start": 2551,
"char_end": 2613,
"unit_id": "t0017.u01",
"sent_id": "t0017.s03"
},
{
"start": 203.722,
"end": 207.325,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "I've observed this pattern in three different teams.",
"char_start": 2614,
"char_end": 2666,
"unit_id": "t0017.u01",
"sent_id": "t0017.s04"
},
{
"start": 207.325,
"end": 208.747,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "Give me a specific example.",
"char_start": 2681,
"char_end": 2708,
"unit_id": "t0018.u01",
"sent_id": "t0018.s01"
},
{
"start": 208.747,
"end": 213.593,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "What did you used to believe about that, and what have you revised your views on since then?",
"char_start": 2709,
"char_end": 2801,
"unit_id": "t0018.u01",
"sent_id": "t0018.s02"
},
{
"start": 213.593,
"end": 221.783,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "Yes, so \u2013 a bike should feel quiet and predictable, so that your attention remains focused on the trail.",
"char_start": 2817,
"char_end": 2921,
"unit_id": "t0019.u01",
"sent_id": "t0019.s01"
},
{
"start": 221.783,
"end": 226.902,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "Once you understand that, the other decisions will become easier.",
"char_start": 2922,
"char_end": 2987,
"unit_id": "t0019.u01",
"sent_id": "t0019.s02"
},
{
"start": 226.902,
"end": 227.749,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "Let's start there.",
"char_start": 3002,
"char_end": 3020,
"unit_id": "t0020.u01",
"sent_id": "t0020.s01"
},
{
"start": 227.749,
"end": 232.078,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "What did you used to believe about that, and what have you revised your views on since then?",
"char_start": 3021,
"char_end": 3113,
"unit_id": "t0020.u01",
"sent_id": "t0020.s02"
},
{
"start": 232.078,
"end": 233.676,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "That's my perspective.",
"char_start": 3129,
"char_end": 3151,
"unit_id": "t0021.u01",
"sent_id": "t0021.s01"
},
{
"start": 233.676,
"end": 239.558,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "Chain wear is the best early indicator of when you need to replace your cassette.",
"char_start": 3152,
"char_end": 3233,
"unit_id": "t0021.u01",
"sent_id": "t0021.s02"
},
{
"start": 239.558,
"end": 243.553,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "We've seen this with teams that use Shimano components.",
"char_start": 3234,
"char_end": 3289,
"unit_id": "t0021.u01",
"sent_id": "t0021.s03"
},
{
"start": 243.553,
"end": 247.91,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "Once you understand that, the other decisions become easier.",
"char_start": 3290,
"char_end": 3350,
"unit_id": "t0021.u01",
"sent_id": "t0021.s04"
},
{
"start": 247.91,
"end": 248.637,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "That fits.\nThat works.\nThat's perfect.\nThat's right.\nThat's a good fit.",
"char_start": 3365,
"char_end": 3436,
"unit_id": "t0022.u01",
"sent_id": "t0022.s01"
},
{
"start": 248.637,
"end": 258.995,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "And when teams adopt the Spoke & Wrench process, the compromises become apparent. If you ignore these compromises, you'll end up having to rebuild everything from scratch a year later.",
"char_start": 3452,
"char_end": 3636,
"unit_id": "t0023.u01",
"sent_id": "t0023.s01"
},
{
"start": 258.995,
"end": 260.271,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "Let's start there.",
"char_start": 3651,
"char_end": 3669,
"unit_id": "t0024.u01",
"sent_id": "t0024.s01"
},
{
"start": 260.271,
"end": 265.728,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "What is the operational perspective that most listeners don't have access to?",
"char_start": 3670,
"char_end": 3747,
"unit_id": "t0024.u01",
"sent_id": "t0024.s02"
},
{
"start": 265.728,
"end": 267.018,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "That's how I see it.",
"char_start": 3763,
"char_end": 3783,
"unit_id": "t0025.u01",
"sent_id": "t0025.s01"
},
{
"start": 267.018,
"end": 272.757,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "The service intervals for the suspension are a decision made by the risk management team.",
"char_start": 3784,
"char_end": 3873,
"unit_id": "t0025.u01",
"sent_id": "t0025.s02"
},
{
"start": 272.757,
"end": 276.24,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "I have observed this pattern in three different teams.",
"char_start": 3874,
"char_end": 3928,
"unit_id": "t0025.u01",
"sent_id": "t0025.s03"
},
{
"start": 276.24,
"end": 281.615,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "Let's change the subject \u2013 I want to dedicate the final section to risk management.",
"char_start": 3943,
"char_end": 4026,
"unit_id": "t0026.u01",
"sent_id": "t0026.s01"
},
{
"start": 281.615,
"end": 289.811,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "That's where the conversation becomes interesting, because the compromises regarding risk management permeate everything we've discussed.",
"char_start": 4042,
"char_end": 4179,
"unit_id": "t0027.u01",
"sent_id": "t0027.s01"
},
{
"start": 289.811,
"end": 291.85,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "Give me a specific example.",
"char_start": 4194,
"char_end": 4221,
"unit_id": "t0028.u01",
"sent_id": "t0028.s01"
},
{
"start": 291.85,
"end": 296.381,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "What is the most underestimated part of the drive mechanism?",
"char_start": 4222,
"char_end": 4282,
"unit_id": "t0028.u01",
"sent_id": "t0028.s02"
},
{
"start": 296.381,
"end": 297.112,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "Certainly.",
"char_start": 4298,
"char_end": 4308,
"unit_id": "t0029.u01",
"sent_id": "t0029.s01"
},
{
"start": 297.112,
"end": 306.249,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "Most mysterious creaking noises can be resolved by cleaning the contact surfaces and tightening them to the specified torque.",
"char_start": 4309,
"char_end": 4434,
"unit_id": "t0029.u01",
"sent_id": "t0029.s02"
},
{
"start": 306.249,
"end": 310.488,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "We've seen this happen with teams that use Spoke & Wrench.",
"char_start": 4435,
"char_end": 4493,
"unit_id": "t0029.u01",
"sent_id": "t0029.s03"
},
{
"start": 310.488,
"end": 314.289,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "I've observed this pattern in three different teams.",
"char_start": 4494,
"char_end": 4546,
"unit_id": "t0029.u01",
"sent_id": "t0029.s04"
},
{
"start": 314.289,
"end": 316.296,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "This is a useful framework.",
"char_start": 4561,
"char_end": 4588,
"unit_id": "t0030.u01",
"sent_id": "t0030.s01"
},
{
"start": 316.296,
"end": 321.796,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "What is the opposing perspective that most listeners are unable to access?",
"char_start": 4589,
"char_end": 4663,
"unit_id": "t0030.u01",
"sent_id": "t0030.s02"
},
{
"start": 321.796,
"end": 330.003,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "Ultimately, a bike should feel quiet and predictable, so that your attention remains focused on the trail.",
"char_start": 4679,
"char_end": 4785,
"unit_id": "t0031.u01",
"sent_id": "t0031.s01"
},
{
"start": 330.003,
"end": 335.888,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "The frame is important because it tells you what compromises you are making.",
"char_start": 4786,
"char_end": 4862,
"unit_id": "t0031.u01",
"sent_id": "t0031.s02"
},
{
"start": 335.888,
"end": 338.298,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "What does the error scenario look like?",
"char_start": 4877,
"char_end": 4916,
"unit_id": "t0032.u01",
"sent_id": "t0032.s01"
},
{
"start": 338.298,
"end": 342.005,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "What is the most underestimated part of the drive mechanism?",
"char_start": 4917,
"char_end": 4977,
"unit_id": "t0032.u01",
"sent_id": "t0032.s02"
},
{
"start": 342.005,
"end": 348.929,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "To be honest, chain wear is the best early indicator of when you need to replace your cassette.",
"char_start": 4993,
"char_end": 5088,
"unit_id": "t0033.u01",
"sent_id": "t0033.s01"
},
{
"start": 348.929,
"end": 352.938,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "We've seen this with teams that use Shimano components.",
"char_start": 5089,
"char_end": 5144,
"unit_id": "t0033.u01",
"sent_id": "t0033.s02"
},
{
"start": 352.938,
"end": 356.728,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "I've observed this pattern in three different teams.",
"char_start": 5145,
"char_end": 5197,
"unit_id": "t0033.u01",
"sent_id": "t0033.s03"
},
{
"start": 356.728,
"end": 358.201,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "Where does it break down?",
"char_start": 5212,
"char_end": 5237,
"unit_id": "t0034.u01",
"sent_id": "t0034.s01"
},
{
"start": 358.201,
"end": 367.391,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "And when teams adopt this process from Shimano, the compromise becomes apparent \u2013 I've observed this pattern in three different teams.",
"char_start": 5253,
"char_end": 5387,
"unit_id": "t0035.u01",
"sent_id": "t0035.s01"
},
{
"start": 367.391,
"end": 370.801,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "What is the heuristic that you always fall back on?",
"char_start": 5402,
"char_end": 5453,
"unit_id": "t0036.u01",
"sent_id": "t0036.s01"
},
{
"start": 370.801,
"end": 374.345,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "Where do maintenance and the drive mechanism overlap?",
"char_start": 5454,
"char_end": 5507,
"unit_id": "t0036.u01",
"sent_id": "t0036.s02"
},
{
"start": 374.345,
"end": 381.055,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "To be honest, service intervals for the suspension are a decision made by the risk management team.",
"char_start": 5523,
"char_end": 5622,
"unit_id": "t0037.u01",
"sent_id": "t0037.s01"
},
{
"start": 381.055,
"end": 385.529,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "And the second-order effect is the part that most people overlook.",
"char_start": 5623,
"char_end": 5689,
"unit_id": "t0037.u01",
"sent_id": "t0037.s02"
},
{
"start": 385.529,
"end": 390.98,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "Before we wrap up, is there one thing that listeners can try out this week?",
"char_start": 5704,
"char_end": 5779,
"unit_id": "t0038.u01",
"sent_id": "t0038.s01"
},
{
"start": 390.98,
"end": 396.373,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "Choose one of the ideas we discussed and implement it for two weeks.",
"char_start": 5795,
"char_end": 5863,
"unit_id": "t0039.u01",
"sent_id": "t0039.s01"
},
{
"start": 396.373,
"end": 398.118,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "The rest is iteration.",
"char_start": 5864,
"char_end": 5886,
"unit_id": "t0039.u01",
"sent_id": "t0039.s02"
},
{
"start": 398.118,
"end": 403.644,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "Before we close, I'd like to thank our friends at Linear once again.",
"char_start": 5901,
"char_end": 5969,
"unit_id": "t0040.u01",
"sent_id": "t0040.s01"
},
{
"start": 403.644,
